Per-item logs

Each item writes only its own files:

- logs/<Item>-build.log — `Build completed successfully ...` for the package build that recorded that item, then exit=
- logs/<Item>-print-axioms.log — `#print axioms` lines for that item, then exit=

The item name is the module after `ExistenceSystem` in the declaration name.

Do not append to a shared logs/lake-build.log or logs/print-axioms.log.
A branch records one item, and does not rewrite the others:

    checks/item-logs.sh KL13

With no argument, checks/item-logs.sh records every item in checks/PrintAxioms.lean.
Append a fully qualified `#print axioms ExistenceSystem.<Item>.<decl>` line there.
The axiom bar is propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.
